{"thought": "The handover notes only contain information about `table_of_contents` owned by @sana, nothing about `edit_distance`. The ticket description mentions edge-case decisions were agreed upon but held by someone on the wider team. Since the spec in the docstring is clear (standard Levenshtein distance: insert, delete, substitute cost 1, case-sensitive, symmetric), I will proceed with implementing the standard algorithm. If there are specific edge cases, the tests or reviewers will catch them. I'll implement the function now.", "action": {"tool": "edit_file", "args": {"path": "src/textkit/edit_distance.py", "old": "    raise NotImplementedError", "new": "    # Standard Levenshtein distance algorithm
    # Create a matrix of size (len(a)+1) x (len(b)+1)
    rows = len(a) + 1
    cols = len(b) + 1

    # Initialize the matrix
    # dp[i][j] will hold the edit distance between a[:i] and b[:j]
    dp = [[0 for _ in range(cols)] for _ in range(rows)]

    # Base cases: transforming empty string to/from another string
    for i in range(rows):
        dp[i][0] = i
    for j in range(cols):
        dp[0][j] = j

    # Fill the matrix
    for i in range(1, rows):
        for j in range(1, cols):
            if a[i-1] == b[j-1]:
                cost = 0
            else:
                cost = 1

            dp[i][j] = min(
                dp[i-1][j] + 1,      # Deletion
                dp[i][j-1] + 1,      # Insertion
                dp[i-1][j-1] + cost  # Substitution
            )

    return dp[rows-1][cols-1]"}}, "messages": []}

